==
\n

I am a Senior ML Scientist at Amazon Web Services, where I lead the research, design, and productionization of adaptive machine-learning and agentic systems. I originated and led the science behind [https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/rds-protection.html GuardDuty for RDS Protection], an unsupervised online system that adapts to each customer and changing data. More recently, I have set technical direction for agent memory, orchestration, evaluation, personal knowledge graphs, and structured-data capabilities shipped across Amazon Quick and the SageMaker assistant. \n

*Trajectory* \n

Before AWS, I was a  post-doctoral researcher at University of California, Berkeley, hosted by [https://people.eecs.berkeley.edu/~ananth/?_ga=2.265916295.944206018.1658767219-220427129.1570763517 Venkat Anantharam]. I received my PhD ([defense_slides.pdf thesis defense]) from The University of Texas at Austin, where  I was affiliated with the [https://www.ma.utexas.edu/simons/ Simons Center for Network Mathematics ] and advised by [http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/baccelli/ François Baccelli]. I was also fortunate to collaborate and learn from [https://sites.google.com/view/sanjay-shakkottai/home Sanjay Shakkottai], [https://researchportal.hw.ac.uk/en/persons/sergey-foss Sergey Foss], [http://users.ece.utexas.edu/~hvikalo/ Haris Vikalo] during grad school. I spent my childhood years in Bengaluru with my brother [http://karthikabinavs.xyz/ Karthik Abinav Sankararaman] before completing an undergraduate degree from IIT Madras.



